      "label": "Description",
      "searchable": true,
      "value": "Prime Minister Jim Bolger at the podium in Papakura, September 1993. To his left is a larger-than-life size poster of local MP John Robertson.\"Prime Minister Jim Bolger was in Papakura last week launching the National Party's health policy. Some points in the health policy include improving child health services, improving the health of Maori and Pacific Islanders and improving mental health services. Other health priorities are to look at hospice services, rehabilitation services and replacing waiting lists with a booking service. After launching the policy he then visited Middlemore Hospital to see first hand the problems with the health system.\" (Papakura Courier, 29 September 1993, p. 5)"
